**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# Host build output: 150+ MB and 11k files that every build context carried for nothing. It also
# kept builds from being hermetic — the WebClient image installs its own dependencies and then
# copies the source over them, layering a host node_modules on top of the container's.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
.git/
.github/
*.md

# A Daemon's state directory holds the private key that IS that machine's identity. Both
# Dockerfiles copy the whole tree into the build stage, so without this every local build
# pulls real machine keys into the build context and its layer cache — they never reach the
# final image, but a cache export or a pushed build stage would carry them out.
src/Daemon/state*/

# azd's per-environment state, including values that should not be baked into an image.
.azure/

# Terraform plan output can embed state values.
*.tfplan
